-- title:
--   Positions, the frictional mean-variance objective (4.1) and optimal trading rates
-- statement:
--   An agent with risk aversion $\gamma^n$, initial position $\varphi^n_{0-}\in\mathbb R^K$ and endowment volatility $\xi^n$ who trades at rate $\dot\varphi$ holds $\varphi_t=\varphi^n_{0-}+\int_0^t\dot\varphi_u\,du$ and receives the **frictional goal functional**
--
--   $$J^n_T(\dot\varphi)=\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^T\Big(\varphi_t^\top\mu_t-\frac{\gamma^n}2\|\sigma_t^\top\varphi_t+\xi^n_t\|^2-\frac12\dot\varphi_t^\top\Lambda\dot\varphi_t\Big)dt\Big]\qquad(4.1)$$
--
--   for price dynamics $dS_t=\mu_t\,dt+\sigma_t\,dW_t$ and transaction cost matrix $\Lambda$. A rate is **admissible** if it lies in $\mathbb H^4(\mathbb R^K)$, and an admissible rate $\dot\varphi^*$ is **optimal** if $J^n_T(\dot\varphi)\le J^n_T(\dot\varphi^*)$ for every admissible $\dot\varphi$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The expectation and the time integral are Bochner integrals. Whenever $\mu\in\mathbb H^2$, $\sigma\in\mathbb H^4$ and $\xi^n\in\mathbb H^2$ (the situation of every theorem in this mission), the integrand is integrable for every admissible rate, because $\sup_t\|\varphi_t\|\in L^4$ (footnote 6); so Lean's junk value $0$ for non-integrable functions never decides optimality. No integrability is added to admissibility.
-- source:
--   Muhle-Karbe–Shi–Yang, An Equilibrium Model for the Cross-Section of Liquidity Premia, arXiv:2011.13625v1, eq. (4.1) and footnote 6, p.5; eq. (4.4), p.6

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LiqPremiaEq_opNorm
import Definitions.Def_LiqPremiaEq_IsHp

open MeasureTheory Matrix
open scoped NNReal

namespace LiqPremiaEq

/-- The position `φ_t = φ_{0−} + ∫₀ᵗ φ̇_u du` generated by a trading rate `φ̇` from the initial
position `φ_{0−}` (pathwise).
Muhle-Karbe–Shi–Yang, arXiv:2011.13625v1, Section 4, p.5 ("absolutely continuous with rate φ̇")
and eq. (4.4), p.6. -/
noncomputable def position {Ω : Type*} {K : ℕ} (x0 : Fin K → ℝ)
    (rate : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : Fin K → ℝ :=
  x0 + ∫ u in Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) t, rate u.toNNReal ω

/-- The frictional mean-variance goal functional of an agent with risk aversion `γⁿ`, initial
position `φ_{0−}` and endowment volatility `ξⁿ`, for a trading rate `φ̇`:
`Jⁿ_T(φ̇) = E[∫₀ᵀ (φ_tᵀμ_t − (γⁿ/2)‖σ_tᵀφ_t + ξⁿ_t‖² − ½ φ̇_tᵀΛφ̇_t) dt]`.
Muhle-Karbe–Shi–Yang, arXiv:2011.13625v1, eq. (4.1), p.5.

**Formalization Note** `‖·‖` is the Euclidean norm (`frobVec`). The expectation and the time
integral are Bochner integrals. For every admissible rate (`Hᴴ⁴`, see `IsOptimalRate`), with
`μ ∈ H²`, `σ ∈ H⁴` and `ξⁿ ∈ H²`, the integrand is `P ⊗ dt`-integrable (footnote 6, p.5:
`sup_t ‖φ_t‖ ∈ L⁴` by Cauchy–Schwarz), so the integral never takes Lean's junk value on a
competitor in the theorems of this mission. -/
noncomputable def objective {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {K D : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (T : ℝ≥0) (γn : ℝ) (Λ : Matrix (Fin K) (Fin K) ℝ) (x0 : Fin K → ℝ)
    (ξn : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin D → ℝ) (μ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ)
    (σ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Matrix (Fin K) (Fin D) ℝ) (rate : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, (∫ s in Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T,
    (position x0 rate s.toNNReal ω ⬝ᵥ μ s.toNNReal ω
      - γn / 2 * frobVec ((σ s.toNNReal ω)ᵀ *ᵥ position x0 rate s.toNNReal ω
          + ξn s.toNNReal ω) ^ 2
      - 1 / 2 * (rate s.toNNReal ω ⬝ᵥ (Λ *ᵥ rate s.toNNReal ω)))) ∂P

/-- A trading rate `φ̇*` is **optimal** for the frictional problem (4.1) of an agent: it is
admissible, i.e. `φ̇* ∈ H⁴(ℝᴷ)`, and `Jⁿ_T(φ̇) ≤ Jⁿ_T(φ̇*)` for every admissible rate `φ̇`.
Muhle-Karbe–Shi–Yang, arXiv:2011.13625v1, eq. (4.1) and the sentence after it, p.5
("we focus on admissible trading strategies that are absolutely continuous with rate
φ̇ ∈ H⁴(ℝᴷ)").

**Formalization Note** Admissibility is exactly membership in `H⁴` (progressively measurable on
`[0, T]` with `E[(∫₀ᵀ‖φ̇_t‖²dt)²] < ∞`); no integrability of the objective is added, so the
competitor set is the paper's. -/
def IsOptimalRate {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] {K D : ℕ}
    (𝓕 : MeasureTheory.Filtration ℝ≥0 mΩ) (P : Measure Ω) (T : ℝ≥0) (γn : ℝ)
    (Λ : Matrix (Fin K) (Fin K) ℝ) (x0 : Fin K → ℝ) (ξn : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin D → ℝ)
    (μ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ) (σ : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Matrix (Fin K) (Fin D) ℝ)
    (rate : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ) : Prop :=
  IsHp 𝓕 P T 4 rate ∧
    ∀ rate' : ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin K → ℝ, IsHp 𝓕 P T 4 rate' →
      objective P T γn Λ x0 ξn μ σ rate' ≤ objective P T γn Λ x0 ξn μ σ rate

end LiqPremiaEq


